{"id": "EUVD-2026-82069", "enisaUuid": "f21021ec-1ece-37c9-aaee-6452e9ef3089", "description": "In the Linux kernel, the following vulnerability has been resolved:\n\nwifi: ath12k: fix overreads in ath12k_wmi_process_csa_switch_count_event()\n\nThere is no policy entry for WMI_TAG_PDEV_CSA_SWITCH_COUNT_STATUS_EVENT, so\nthe parse infrastructure does not enforce a minimum length for the event\nstruct. Additionally, the num_vdevs field is taken directly from firmware\nand used as a loop bound over the vdev_ids array without checking that it\nfits within the TLV payload. Either condition can cause an out-of-bounds\nread.\n\nAdd a TLV policy entry for WMI_TAG_PDEV_CSA_SWITCH_COUNT_STATUS_EVENT so\nthe parse infrastructure enforces a minimum length for the fixed-size event\nstruct. Add a helper ath12k_wmi_tlv_data_len() to recover the payload\nlength of a parsed TLV from the header preceding its data pointer. Use it\nin ath12k_wmi_process_csa_switch_count_event() to bound num_vdevs before\nthe loop.\n\nCompile tested only.", "datePublished": "2026-09-17T16:09:36", "dateUpdated": "2026-10-21T12:51:31", "baseScore": 7.7, "baseScoreVersion": "3.1", "baseScoreVector": "CVSS:3.1/AV:L/AC:L/PR:N/UI:N/S:U/C:H/I:N/A:H", "references": ["https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/d4aec20f3a84634171c139ab2e02bb2e5a5c756b", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/24f7cdabea9f7ab95dbd6d8bc9ac6ec48d96a7e5", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/23bed4ef132c55c9016f0c6122c8b8ba2efa2353", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/bf97c9d5123859a07848462539153176db029f3a", "https://git.kernel.org/stable/c/878654eb78c6aa0ff585baf1376567c775ca28ec"], "aliases": ["CVE-2026-90408", "GHSA-f527-4pqf-x9g9"], "assigner": "Linux", "epss": 0.19, "enisaIdProduct": [{"id": "0fc33ff0-88f3-3d5e-82cc-dcbc93298710", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d889913205cf7ebda905b1e62c5867ed4e39f6c2 <24f7cdabea9f7ab95dbd6d8bc9ac6ec48d96a7e5"}, {"id": "2117f4bc-a320-36ce-8d47-5ccd6cdc16e8", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d889913205cf7ebda905b1e62c5867ed4e39f6c2 <878654eb78c6aa0ff585baf1376567c775ca28ec"}, {"id": "3930adbf-19ef-3152-8914-805621782492", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.6.160"}, {"id": "3c8e5453-f7a4-31c7-9d97-3909d11ace4b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.3"}, {"id": "4842d5d2-b66b-350a-b69d-b08b1bbe2f03", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d889913205cf7ebda905b1e62c5867ed4e39f6c2 <23bed4ef132c55c9016f0c6122c8b8ba2efa2353"}, {"id": "4be3370f-c235-328c-b4b8-3d475e8c8951", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d889913205cf7ebda905b1e62c5867ed4e39f6c2 <bf97c9d5123859a07848462539153176db029f3a"}, {"id": "7868d332-1654-346c-bfa9-ca28ec6cf63b", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "d889913205cf7ebda905b1e62c5867ed4e39f6c2 <d4aec20f3a84634171c139ab2e02bb2e5a5c756b"}, {"id": "86b00394-c8be-3193-a038-ee5146db6b0d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.18.57"}, {"id": "a679229c-6150-392f-9f4b-496cb39d405d", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 7.2.6"}, {"id": "c089bc63-5b7c-3250-bd3a-3877b1caf0a6", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 6.12.114"}, {"id": "c5a06e9a-4488-3c15-aa6b-3c13b54a14a7", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "patch: 0"}, {"id": "ccbebfda-5b34-3f0f-aed0-017a22d7c265", "product": {"name": "Linux", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}, "product_version": "6.3"}], "enisaIdVendor": [{"id": "b1aecb71-c067-3ec1-8d14-ab60a178c98f", "vendor": {"name": "Linux"}}], "isExploited": false}